## For your WorkerHub project

Your proposed structure is already moving toward an AI-friendly architecture:

```text
features/
services/
hooks/
types/
```

That's good.

The one thing I'd add is:

```text
docs/
  architecture.md
  conventions.md
```

and keep them short.

Because AI doesn't struggle most with code.

It struggles with:

> "How do the humans want this project organized?"

If you answer that once in a document, every future AI session becomes more consistent.

A useful rule of thumb:

> If a new developer could understand where to make a change in 5 minutes, an AI will usually perform well there too. If a new developer would be lost, the AI will be lost faster.
